<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Evaluations of sampling methods against baseline categories (Vanilla and Best-of-N) on various metrics for DeepSeek-7B. We evaluate on three distinct task categories. For Perplexity (PPL), lower is better (<math id="S5.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>); for all other metrics, higher is better (<math id="S5.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>). RM: Reward Model Score. Div.: Diversity. Coh.: Coherence. Datasets used are HarmfulQA, IMDB, and GSM-8k for Harmlessness, Positive Sentiment, and Improved Mathematical Reasoning Alignment, respectively.</figcaption>
