</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span><span id="S6.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> on Small Models Beats Large Models</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We benchmark a suite of small (<math id="S6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math>7B) models against the powerful <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Llama-405B</span> model on the <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HH-RLHF</span> dataset. As shown in Table <a href="#S6.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 6.2 AdaSearch Outperforms Model Fine-tuning ‣ 6 Experimental Results ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the small vanilla models are generally outperformed by <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Llama-405B</span>, confirming its superior baseline alignment. Applying the Best-of-N baseline proves insufficient to close this gap and, in some cases, even degrades performance (e.g., for Mistral-7B). In contrast, equipping the same small models with <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay leads to a significant improvement. For instance, <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Mistral-7B</span>’s win-rate increases from 43.82% to 73.77%, and even the fine-tuned <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Llama-8B-DPO</span> model’s win-rate climbs from 70.90% to 84.77%. We attribute this to the decaying sampling schedule in <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay, as the initial set of tokens is the most critical for harmlessness alignment.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Win-rates (%) of different AdaSearch schedules generalized to beam search on the HH-RLHF dataset. The Decay schedule consistently outperforms both Uniform and Growth schedules, validating our core hypothesis.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T4.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T4.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.8pt;padding-right:2.8pt;"></th>
<th id="S6.T4.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.8pt;padding-right:2.8pt;" colspan="3"><span id="S6.T4.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">AdaBeam</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:2.8pt;padding-right:2.8pt;"><span id="S6.T4.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Model</span></th>
<th id="S6.T4.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.8pt;padding-right:2.8pt;"><span id="S6.T4.4.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Decay</span></th>
<th id="S6.T4.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.8pt;padding-right:2.8pt;"><span id="S6.T4.4.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Uniform (Tree-BON)</span></th>
<th id="S6.T4.4.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.8pt;padding-right:2.8pt;"><span id="S6.T4.4.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Growth</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T4.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.8pt;padding-right:2.8pt;"><span id="S6.T4.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LLAMA-3.1-8B</span></th>
