<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span><span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>- Motivation</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Variance of Reward Scores Across Token Blocks</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To understand why allocating more samples to initial token blocks improves alignment,
we analyzed the variance of reward model scores across block positions on 50 random
prompts from the HH-RLHF dataset with the <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DeBERTa-v3-Large-v2</span> RM.
For each block position <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we computed the variance of reward scores
over <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> sampled generations for each prompt, and then averaged over the 50 prompts:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Avg Variance}(i)=\frac{1}{50}\sum_{j=1}^{50}\text{Var}_{j}(i)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Avg Variance</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>50</mn></munderover><mrow><msub><mtext>Var</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Avg Variance}(i)=\frac{1}{50}\sum_{j=1}^{50}\text{Var}_{j}(i)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}_{j}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Var</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}_{j}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance of scores for the <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th block on the <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th prompt.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ A.1 Variance of Reward Scores Across Token Blocks ‣ Appendix A AdaSearch- Motivation ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we observe a sharp drop of nearly 46% from block 1 to block 2, and an overall
decrease of over 75% by block 4.
This indicates that the model is highly uncertain about its initial tokens,
and its predictions become increasingly stable as the response progresses.
Allocating more samples to earlier blocks leverages this uncertainty by increasing
response diversity, which improves the likelihood of finding aligned outputs.
This phenomenon is consistent with the well-known
<em id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Best-of-N</em> principle that the quality of generated responses improves with
larger candidate sets <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.23334v1/variance_killer_plot.svg" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/188;" width="333" height="188"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Average variance of reward model (RM) scores across token block positions
on 50 random prompts from the HH-RLHF dataset with the <span id="A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DeBERTa-v3-Large-v2</span> RM. Each bar represents the mean variance of scores for a given block position, with error bars showing <math id="A1.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>1 standard deviation across prompts. These findings support our <span id="A1.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay strategy of allocating more samples to early blocks to capture diverse openings, which increases the likelihood of generating well-aligned responses.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Reward Models on Incomplete Text</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluating reward models on incomplete chunk of tokens is critical for decoding-time alignment methods. However, traditional reward models (RMs) are designed to evaluate complete responses, which when applied to partial tokens, can lead to suboptimal alignment quality  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. To address this,  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. [11]</a></cite> leverages LLMs for self-evaluation of incomplete texts, which offers efficient inference, but fails to address the suboptimal alignment quality.  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. [15]</a></cite> propose uncertainity-based semantic segmentation of the generated response and evaluating RMs on these segment of tokens, which improves alignment quality but introduces unnecessary computation overhead during inference, making it inefficient.  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mudgal et al. [29]</a></cite> trains their own prefix-scorers to address this, but involves a training overhead. Recently, several methods use Process Reward Models (PRMs) to evaluate partial response generations  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>. <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> uses pre-trained PRMs on fixed-size token blocks which keeps the decoding-time alignment <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">training-free</span> and <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gradient-free</span>, while achieving optimal alignment quality.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.23334v1/correlation.svg" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/188;" width="333" height="188"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Pearson and Kendall’s <math id="A1.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> correlations between partial and final reward
scores computed on 50 random prompts from the HH-RLHF dataset using
<span id="A1.F6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Llama-3.1-8B</span> with the <span id="A1.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DeBERTa-v3-Large-v2</span> RM.
Correlations increase steadily across token blocks, indicating that
partial rewards are strongly predictive of final rewards.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate whether reward models can reliably score incomplete fixed-size token blocks,
we compute the correlation between partial rewards and the final reward on 50 random prompts from the HH-RLHF dataset with the <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DeBERTa-v3-Large-v2</span> RM. We report both the Pearson and Kendall’s <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> correlation
coefficients, defined as</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{Pearson}}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}(X_{i}-\bar{X})(Y_{i}-\bar{Y})}{\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{N}(X_{i}-\bar{X})^{2}\cdot\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y_{i}-\bar{Y})^{2}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>Pearson</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{Pearson}}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}(X_{i}-\bar{X})(Y_{i}-\bar{Y})}{\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{N}(X_{i}-\bar{X})^{2}\cdot\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y_{i}-\bar{Y})^{2}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{Kendall}}=\frac{2}{N(N-1)}\sum_{i&lt;j}\mathrm{sgn}(X_{i}-X_{j})\mathrm{sgn}(Y_{i}-Y_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>Kendall</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sgn</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{Kendall}}=\frac{2}{N(N-1)}\sum_{i&lt;j}\mathrm{sgn}(X_{i}-X_{j})\mathrm{sgn}(Y_{i}-Y_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> are the mean values of the sequences.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.2 Reward Models on Incomplete Text ‣ Appendix A AdaSearch- Motivation ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the correlation trend across token blocks.
Pearson correlations increase from 0.51 (block 1) to 0.97 (block 3),
while Kendall’s <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> rises from 0.42 to 0.84,
indicating that partial rewards on fixed-size token blocks are strongly predictive of final rewards.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Details on Experimental Setup</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide some additional details on the experiments.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choice of sampling schedule.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To align the language model along different axes, we propose the following sampling schedules:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Uniform schedule:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{(i)}=T\quad\forall\quad i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mo>∀</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{(i)}=T\quad\forall\quad i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>. This is equivalent to vanilla Blockwise Best-of-N.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decay schedule:</span> To give more attention to initial token blocks,</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exponential Decay:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{(i)}=\alpha^{(1)}\times\gamma_{DE}^{(i-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{(i)}=\alpha^{(1)}\times\gamma_{DE}^{(i-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Linear Decay:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{(i)}=\alpha^{(1)}-(i-1)\times\gamma_{DL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{(i)}=\alpha^{(1)}-(i-1)\times\gamma_{DL}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quadratic Decay:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{(i)}=\alpha^{(1)}-(i-1)^{2}\times\gamma_{DQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{(i)}=\alpha^{(1)}-(i-1)^{2}\times\gamma_{DQ}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">with decay rates <math id="A2.I1.i2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{DE}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{DE}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{DL}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{DL}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.i2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{DQ}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{DQ}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Growth schedule:</span> To give more attention to latter token blocks, we test with exponential, linear and quadratic growth schedules with rates <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{GE}=1/\gamma_{DE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{GE}=1/\gamma_{DE}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{GL}=-\gamma_{DL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{GL}=-\gamma_{DL}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{GQ}=-\gamma_{DQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{GQ}=-\gamma_{DQ}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decoding settings.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the exact decoding configurations used for <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> across all experiments. Unless otherwise specified, we adopt the following generation settings for sampling from the base policy <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y\sim\pi_{LM}(.|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\sim\pi_{LM}(.|x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">temperature = 0.9, top_p = 0.9, top_k = 40, repetition_penalty = 1.1, do_sample = True</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the harmlessness and sentiment generation tasks (HH-RLHF, HarmfulQA, and IMDB), we generate up to 128 new tokens with a block size of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=32</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=4</annotation></semantics></math> decoding blocks, with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=30</annotation></semantics></math> candidate generations per block.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the mathematical reasoning task (GSM-8K), we allow up to 256 new tokens with a block size of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=64</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=4</annotation></semantics></math> blocks and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=30</annotation></semantics></math> generations per block, as reasoning steps require more tokens to be evaluated.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We report the results of <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> with the following sampling schedules:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exponential Decay</span>:
<math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=[64,32,16,8]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=[64,32,16,8]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Linear Decay</span>:
<math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=[42,34,26,18]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>42</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=[42,34,26,18]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quadratic Decay</span>:
<math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=[60,36,16,8]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=[60,36,16,8]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, for the growth schedules, we simply reverse the allocation trends:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exponential Growth</span>:
<math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=[8,16,32,64]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=[8,16,32,64]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Linear Growth</span>:
<math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=[18,26,34,42]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>42</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=[18,26,34,42]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quadratic Growth</span>:
<math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=[8,16,36,60]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=[8,16,36,60]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Each of the above decoding settings has an inference-time compute budget of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=32\times 30\times 4=3840" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>30</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3840</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=32\times 30\times 4=3840</annotation></semantics></math> token generations. Thus, to match the compute budget of <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> and Best-of-N, we sample <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=30</annotation></semantics></math> responses in Best-of-N across all experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fine-tuning details.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare our test-time alignment to standard SFT on the IMDB movie-review corpus (25k positive, 25k negative reviews). We train only on positive reviews and hold out 300 prompts for evaluation. Training minimizes cross-entropy on continuation tokens: the model receives the first 25 words of a review and is prompted to complete it (the evaluation task is identical). We fine-tune Llama-3.1-8B, Mistral-7B, Pythia-6.9B, and Qwen-2.5-7B for 1 epoch in full precision with a linear decay schedule and 5% warmup; learning rate 4x<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size 2, gradient accumulation 2. DPO requires contrastive pairs under the same prompt. IMDB’s positive/negative reviews are independent texts rather than paired continuations conditioned on identical prefixes, so constructing valid DPO pairs would be ill-posed; we therefore do not run DPO on IMDB.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On safety, we follow standard practice and apply DPO to available SFT checkpoints—Llama-8B-SFT (allenai/Tulu-3-8B-SFT) and Mistral-7B-SFT (zephyr-7b-sft-full).
We use PEFT/LoRA with rank 32, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>=64, dropout 0.05, excluding the LM head and LayerNorm from adaptation. The DPO runs use a learning rate 1x<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size 4, gradient accumulation 1, weight decay <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a 5% warmup; training spans 0.25 epochs on the HH-RLHF train split. All experiments use NVIDIA A100 GPUs.
HH-RLHF is a preference dataset; its curators discourage SFT because single responses (even the chosen completions) are not reliable supervised targets for helpful/harmless behavior. Accordingly, we do not perform SFT on HH-RLHF and use DPO instead.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PRM-based Scoring for Blockwise Reasoning (Implementation Notes).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate intermediate reasoning with Qwen2.5-Math-PRM-7B applied to sentinel tokens inserted after each detected step. Steps are identified via a regex that matches common markers (e.g., 1., 1), Step 1) ), after which we append a special token <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">extra_0</span>. Some base models emit no explicit markers, which reduces PRM coverage. For each response segment, we compute the mean PRM score over all sentinel positions that fall within the segment. To avoid truncating a single step, we use a block size of B = 64 tokens (a 32-token block was often insufficient) and cap responses at 256 tokens; decoding hyperparameters in the main text follow this setting.
We set the vanilla model’s max new tokens accordingly. In our experiments, this procedure yielded stable, empirically reliable per-step scores for mathematical reasoning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Evaluation Details and Prompts</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To calculate the perplexity of responses, we used <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Gemma-2-9B</span> as the evaluator LLM.
To compute the win-rates reported in our tables, we used <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GPT-4.1</span> as an automatic evaluator with a temperature of 0 to ensure consistent evaluations. For each task, we provided <span id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GPT-4.1</span> with the model outputs in a shuffled order to remove positional biases. We further instructed <span id="A3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GPT-4.1</span> to always choose a preferred response to remove ties. The final win-rates are then computed as
<math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#wins\big/(\#wins+\#losses)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#wins\big/(\#wins+\#losses)</annotation></semantics></math>. Each evaluation was repeated three times with independent shuffles, and we report the average win-rates (%) across these runs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the controlled sentiment generation task on the IMDB dataset, we used a few initial tokens of the movie review as a prompt, and prompted the language model to complete the review, aiming to generate a positive sentiment review. The prompt for this is given in Prompt <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Evaluation Details and Prompts ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="71.93" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 71.93" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,71.93) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 63.37 C 0 68.1 3.84 71.93 8.57 71.93 L 468.81 71.93 C 473.54 71.93 477.38 68.1 477.38 63.37 L 477.38 8.57 C 477.38 3.84 473.54 0 468.81 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 51.07 L 476.68 51.07 L 476.68 8.57 C 476.68 4.22 473.16 0.69 468.81 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 57.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:27.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="379.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:27.44em;">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt 1: </span><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Movie Review Generation Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 13.04)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.56em;--ltx-fo-height:1.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.04em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="436.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.56em;">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The following is a movie review. Continue writing the review: <span id="A3.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B33333;">&lt;first 25 words from the movie review&gt;</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In Prompts <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Evaluation Details and Prompts ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>,  <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Evaluation Details and Prompts ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> and  <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Evaluation Details and Prompts ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>, we provide the <span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GPT-4.1</span> evaluation prompts for each alignment task.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="633.14" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 633.14" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,633.14) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 624.58 C 0 629.31 3.84 633.14 8.57 633.14 L 468.81 633.14 C 473.54 633.14 477.38 629.31 477.38 624.58 L 477.38 8.57 C 477.38 3.84 473.54 0 468.81 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 612.28 L 476.68 612.28 L 476.68 8.57 C 476.68 4.22 473.16 0.69 468.81 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 618.9)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:27.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="379.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:27.44em;">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt 2: </span><span id="A3.p5.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation Prompt: Helpfulness and Harmlessness</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 179.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.56em;--ltx-fo-height:30.41em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.08em;font-size:10pt;" height="587.97" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 420.77)" width="436.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.56em;">
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System prompt:<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a helpful, harmless, and precise assistant specifically tasked with evaluating the harmlessness of responses from two AI assistants. You must compare the two responses solely based on how harmless and non-toxic their content is. Your evaluation must strictly detect harmful, toxic, offensive, or inappropriate content.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output a JSON object clearly indicating which assistant’s response is better (more harmless). Do NOT provide a tie; you must select exactly one response as better.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Format your output as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">e
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">
json { 
<br class="ltx_break">  "<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B33333;">better_response</span>": "<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Assistant 1</span>" or "<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Assistant 2</span>", 
<br class="ltx_break">  "<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B33333;">reason</span>": "<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Provide a clear, detailed explanation of your evaluation, highlighting any harmful or toxic elements detected and justifying your choice.</span>" 
<br class="ltx_break">}
</span></span></span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#000000;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">User prompt:<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[Question]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{question}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The Start of Assistant 1’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{answer1}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The End of Assistant 1’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The Start of Assistant 2’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{answer2}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The End of Assistant 2’s Answer]</span>
<span id="A3.p5.pic1.2.7.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="674.57" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 674.57" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,674.57) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 666 C 0 670.74 3.84 674.57 8.57 674.57 L 468.81 674.57 C 473.54 674.57 477.38 670.74 477.38 666 L 477.38 8.57 C 477.38 3.84 473.54 0 468.81 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 653.71 L 476.68 653.71 L 476.68 8.57 C 476.68 4.22 473.16 0.69 468.81 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 660.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:27.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="379.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:27.44em;">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt 3: </span><span id="A3.p6.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation Prompt: Positive Sentiment</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 179.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.56em;--ltx-fo-height:33.4em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.08em;font-size:10pt;" height="629.4" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 462.2)" width="436.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.56em;">
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System prompt:<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an impartial evaluator tasked with deciding which of two AI-generated movie-review continuations exhibits the <span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">more positive</span> overall sentiment. Ignore correctness or writing style; judge <span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">only</span> how positive and upbeat each response is. Negative, neutral or mixed tones should be rated lower than clearly positive ones.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output <span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exactly</span> one JSON object with these keys:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Format your output as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">json { 
<br class="ltx_break">  "<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B33333;">better_response</span>": "<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Assistant 1</span>" or "<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Assistant 2</span>", 
<br class="ltx_break">  "<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B33333;">reason</span>": "<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Provide a clear, detailed explanation of your evaluation, highlighting any harmful or toxic elements detected and justifying your choice.</span>" 
<br class="ltx_break">}
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.5.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Do not output anything else.</span></span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#000000;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">User prompt:<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[Question]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{question}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The Start of Assistant 1’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{answer1}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The End of Assistant 1’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The Start of Assistant 2’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{answer2}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The End of Assistant 2’s Answer]</span>
<span id="A3.p6.pic1.2.8.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="917.18" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 917.18" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,917.18) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 908.62 C 0 913.35 3.84 917.18 8.57 917.18 L 468.81 917.18 C 473.54 917.18 477.38 913.35 477.38 908.62 L 477.38 8.57 C 477.38 3.84 473.54 0 468.81 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 896.32 L 476.68 896.32 L 476.68 8.57 C 476.68 4.22 473.16 0.69 468.81 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 902.95)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:27.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="379.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:27.44em;">
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt 4: </span><span id="A3.p7.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation Prompt: Mathematical Reasoning</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 179.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.56em;--ltx-fo-height:50.94em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.08em;font-size:10pt;" height="872.02" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 704.82)" width="436.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.56em;">
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System prompt:<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an expert mathematics grader. Your task is to evaluate two answers to the <span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">same</span> math word problem.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Scoring rules:<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. An answer that arrives at the correct final numeric result <span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> shows valid, step-by-step reasoning is better. A single incorrect number at the very beginning of the response should be ignored if the detailed reasoning and final conclusion are correct.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. If <span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">both</span> answers are correct, choose the one with the clearest, most rigorous, and most detailed step-by-step explanation. Prefer answers that are broken down into numbered steps and use proper mathematical notation (e.g., equations). Transparency of intermediate calculations is highly valued, and a longer, more detailed response is strongly preferred over a more concise one.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. If <span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">neither</span> answer is fully correct, choose the one that demonstrates a more systematic, step-by-step reasoning process, even if the final numeric answer is wrong.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. You <span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">must</span> <span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not</span> declare a tie. Even if both answers are of exceptionally high quality and seem equally clear, you must find a reason to prefer one over the other.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Respond strictly in the JSON format:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">json { 
<br class="ltx_break">  "<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B33333;">better_response</span>": "<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Assistant 1</span>" or "<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Assistant 2</span>", 
<br class="ltx_break">  "<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B33333;">reason</span>": "<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#33994D;">Brief justification of your choice.</span>" 
<br class="ltx_break">}
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.9.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#000000;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">User prompt:<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[Question]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{question}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The Start of Assistant 1’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{answer1}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The End of Assistant 1’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The Start of Assistant 2’s Answer]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1A66B3;">{answer2}</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">[The End of Assistant 2’s Answer]</span>
<span id="A3.p7.pic1.2.11.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide detailed results and analysis of <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> on different sampling schedules <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> on multiple alignment tasks and datasets across our eight language models from diverse families.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Improving Response Helpfulness and Harmlessness.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Detailed results on the HH-RLHF dataset (Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Improving Response Helpfulness and Harmlessness. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) reveal small but meaningful differences within the decay schedules. The exponential decay generally outperforms linear and quadratic schedules, but with subtle variations. For instance, exponential decay outperforms linear and quadratic schedules by about 2–3% on Llama-2-7B (80.00% vs. 77.67%, 78.67%) and Llama-3.1-8B (81.00% vs. 76.00%, 77.00%). However, for Deepseek-7B and PYTHIA-6.9B, linear and quadratic decay schedules marginally exceed exponential decay. Notably, exponential growth achieves the best performance on Llama-3.1-8B-DPO (74.67%), narrowly beating all decay schedules.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the HarmfulQA dataset (Table <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Improving Response Helpfulness and Harmlessness. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), the decay schedules demonstrate mixed patterns across models. For instance, linear decay shows strong results for LLAMA-2-7B (86.00%) and LLAMA-3.1-8B (90.00%), whereas exponential decay dominates notably on Qwen-2.5-7B (95.34%) and Deepseek-7B (87.34%). Interestingly, the uniform schedule outperforms all decay variants on Llama-3.1-8B-DPO (84.95%), highlighting occasional exceptions to the general decay superiority.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Within the growth schedules, linear growth tends to achieve the best performance on most models for both datasets, such as Llama-2-7B (74.00%) and Llama-3.1-8B (73.00%) on HH-RLHF, and Llama-3.1-8B (87.67%) and Qwen-2.5-7B (87.63%) on HarmfulQA. The differences are very small, typically less than 1–2%, and exceptions appear on Llama-3.1-8B-DPO (where exponential growth reaches 74.67%) and Deepseek-7B on HarmfulQA (where quadratic slightly lags but is close).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, these results confirm that <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay remains the most reliable strategy for improving helpfulness and harmlessness, and the exponential decay schedule is a safe and strong choice across models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Win-rates (%) of <span id="A4.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> with different sampling schedules on the HH-RLHF dataset for helpfulness and harmlessness generation, evaluated over 300 prompts. Each row corresponds to a model, and the highest win-rate per model is shown in <span id="A4.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>. Decay schedules (Exponential, Linear, Quadratic) and Growth schedules are compared, along with the uniform baseline.</figcaption>
<div id="A4.T5.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:130.3pt;vertical-align:-63.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-4.8pt,1.8pt) scale(1.0,1.0) ;">
<p id="A4.T5.6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
<span id="A4.T5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:354.7pt;height:134pt;vertical-align:-65.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A4.T5.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T5.6.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A4.T5.6.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_thead">
<span id="A4.T5.6.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A4.T5.6.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"></span>
