<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> vs. SFT. </h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Improving Mathematical Reasoning. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> compares the average <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay performance against models fine-tuned with SFT on the IMDB sentiment generation task. <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay consistently outperforms SFT across all models, often by large margins. For example, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Mistral-7B</span> improves from 59.67% with SFT to 93.00% with <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay, a gain of over 33%. Similarly, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Llama-8B</span> increases from 62.33% to 89.67% (+27.34%), and <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PYTHIA-6.9B</span> improves by 28% (63.00% to 91.00%). Even the weaker <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Qwen-2.5-7B</span> model achieves a substantial gain of +31.62% (52.33% to 83.95%).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These results highlight that <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay can deliver strong alignment performance without the cost of supervised fine-tuning, providing immediate gains with only inference-time adjustments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> vs. DPO.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Improving Mathematical Reasoning. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> compares <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay with Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) on the HH-RLHF dataset. <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay achieves higher win-rates than DPO across both evaluated models, despite operating purely at inference time. For <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Llama-8B-SFT</span>, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay improves from 72.33% with DPO to 78.67%, a gain of approximately 6.3%. Similarly, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Mistral-7B-SFT</span> increases from 80.00% to 81.33% (+1.33%).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These results show that <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span>-Decay can match or even outperform models that have undergone DPO fine-tuning, highlighting its ability to deliver competitive alignment performance without additional training.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Generation examples</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first give all the prompts and responses for Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.3 Blockwise Best-of-N ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> in Table <a href="#A5.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix E Generation examples ‣ Adaptive Blockwise Search: Inference-Time Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. We also provide some example generations by <span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaSearch</span> on various alignment tasks. These responses were generated using the same decoding settings as given and using the exponentially decaying sampling schedule.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T11" class="ltx_table">
